+fingerprints: ["AGENT-2|.claude/hooks/trace-activity.mjs|hook-outcome-unrecorded", "DATA-4|.claude/scripts/render-trace.mjs|reconcile-accepts-any-detail"]
+---
+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U1","attempt":2,"source":"gate","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U1/loop.jsonl:28 gate.coverage (render-trace check ui U1 --stage gates, exit 1, head 9b82b4b): 640e3e1 has no activity record for Agent web-builder","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"AGENT-2","layer":"tests","files":[".claude/hooks/trace-activity.mjs",".claude/settings.json",".claude/hooks/lib/io.mjs",".claude/hooks/guard-bash.mjs",".claude/hooks/guard-agent.mjs"],"root_cause":"The gate is a harness check, not a node rule, so no layer in the schema's enum fits. 'tests' is used because the harness self-test is the test home. AGENT-2 is the nearest rule, because it reads activity.jsonl. What happened: the commit landed. The worktree reflog (.git/worktrees/ui-U1/logs/HEAD:31) has 640e3e1 at 1792615730, which is 20:48:50Z. Yet web-builder a022182fa89499cd2 has no record between activity.jsonl:569 (Edit at 20:43:24Z) and :570 (20:49:34Z). There is no typecheck, no test run, no git add and no git commit in that window. Its first call afterwards, `git log -1 …; git status` (:570) followed by `git rev-parse HEAD` (:571), is a check on whether its commit had landed, which fits its report that hooks blocked some of its Bash calls. The cause is that the trail records tool calls only from trace-activity, and trace-activity runs only on PostToolUse and PostToolUseFailure (settings.json:73-96). A call denied by a PreToolUse guard exits 2 (io.mjs:11-14; guard-bash.mjs:490, guard-agent.mjs:74/81) and never reaches trace-activity. A trace-activity run that is killed (5 s timeout, settings.json:80) or that throws writes only to stderr (trace-activity.mjs:82-83). So the trail holds no record of any hook outcome. The hook itself works when its Post event completes: every other commit on this node got a record 6-7 s after its reflog time (feb65db 20:12:48 → activity.jsonl:438 at 20:12:55; dab4975 20:40:24 → :551 at 20:40:31; 0aa060b 20:51:05 → :582 at 20:51:11). The trail cannot show which mechanism dropped the call that did commit. One candidate is a Post hook killed at its 5 s budget under the parallel W1 and KG4 Playwright load (loop.jsonl:16). The other is a PreToolUse guard timing out and failing open, which would let the command run while the builder saw a hook error. Both are claims, not evidence, and that missing evidence is the cause itself. It recurs: this is the same class as build/F1 762c994 (build/F1/loop.jsonl:55, :60). That fix added PostToolUseFailure, which covers only a call that ran and exited non-zero. It does not cover denials, hook timeouts or a killed Post hook. U0b's four lost records (ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:42-48) were backfilled with no change on the capture side. Both earlier routes treated the symptom. Fix direction (a harness change, so it goes through a harness/<slug> PR, never this node, because of the harness lock): make every hook outcome on a node branch leave a durable trail record. That means a denial record from the PreToolUse guards (agent, agent_id, tool_use_id, redacted command, reason) and a mark when trace-activity fails or is cut short. Also keep the commit-recording path well inside its timeout, so load cannot silently drop a commit record.","fingerprint":"AGENT-2|.claude/hooks/trace-activity.mjs|hook-outcome-unrecorded","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a node branch fixture and a subagent Bash call (agent_id set, agent_type web-builder) that guard-bash or guard-agent denies, When the guard runs and exits 2, Then the node's activity.jsonl gains one record with that agent_id, tool_use_id, the redacted command and the deny reason; and Given trace-activity's commit path on a commit call, When it runs, Then it completes inside its configured timeout (guards.test.mjs / trace.test.mjs, node --test)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"DATA-4","layer":"tests","files":[".claude/scripts/render-trace.mjs"],"root_cause":"The gate is a harness check, so 'tests' is used here for the same reason as I1. The check is honest about the symptom but not about the gap. render-trace.mjs:163-164 asks only whether a commit has a matching activity record. That catches 640e3e1, but it would never notice the builder's missing test runs or its blocked calls. The only exit is reconciledFor (render-trace.mjs:159-162). It accepts any reconciled(activity:<sha7>) event whose detail is non-empty. The tool that writes that event, backfill-activity (render-trace.mjs:418-425), writes agent_id null, tool null and command null, plus a fixed detail: 'the activity record read from git'. Run on 640e3e1, it would turn gate.coverage OK while dropping four facts the trail holds or could hold. First, which dispatched agent made the commit (a022182fa89499cd2, whose other calls are at activity.jsonl:553-571). Second, that its calls from 20:43:24Z to 20:48:50Z (reflog) are missing, not merely the commit. Third, that hooks denied some of its calls. Fourth, that the cause is not known. That breaks DATA-4's agreed interpretation ('Incomplete is never clean') and HONEST-1 (no status that isn't in the trail, which can't be waived). F1's reconciled(activity:0e4fe2f) (build/F1/loop.jsonl:60) carried its cause only because it was written by hand. U0b's backfills (ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:45-48) carry only the generic text, so the earlier route already let a lost record pass with no cause stated. Fix direction: a reconciliation for a lost agent record should carry the evidence, not just exist. That means the agent session id when the trail can attribute it, the window with no records, the commit time from git, and the agent's own report of blocked calls labelled as a claim. The check should refuse a reconciled(activity:…) event whose detail lacks them, rather than accepting any non-empty detail. For this node, the honest route is a backfill that names a022182fa89499cd2, the 20:43:24Z-20:48:50Z window and the unexplained cause. A generic backfill would hide all three.","fingerprint":"DATA-4|.claude/scripts/render-trace.mjs|reconcile-accepts-any-detail","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a fixture trail whose web-builder commit has no activity record while the same agent_id has earlier records, and a reconciled(activity:<sha7>) event whose detail is the generic 'read from git' text with no agent id or window, When render-trace check runs, Then it reports TRAIL INCOMPLETE naming the commit; and Given the same event carrying the agent id, the unrecorded window and the commit time, Then the commit reason clears (trace.test.mjs, node --test)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["10 · A1 · steer(D1,pause1) · David ruling 'U1 takes verdicts'; no investigator dispatched (diagnosed in its own round D1; context only)","13 · A1 · steer(D2,pause1) · web-builder blocked at screen green; David 'Amend tasks' adds t6/t7 compiler red/green; no investigator dispatched (diagnosed in its own round D2; context only)","28 · A1 · gate.coverage FAIL · 640e3e1 has no web-builder activity record (this round, I1 and I2); D1 and D2 have no findings (their own rounds)","32 · A1 · attempt++ → 2","related history outside this node: build/F1 762c994 lost its record when a Bash call exited non-zero; fixed by adding PostToolUseFailure, which does not cover denials or hook timeouts (build/F1/loop.jsonl:55, :60); ui/U0b's four lost main-session records were backfilled with a generic detail (ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:42-48)"]}
