+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U1","attempt":2,"source":"david","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U1/loop.jsonl line 10, steer(D1,pause1)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"NAV-1","layer":"services","files":["src/web/compiler/index.ts","tests/web/unit/compiler/nav-1.test.ts","tests/web/fixtures/trails/rules/README.md"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the real layer is the compiler, one of the ui plan's layers (compiler, loader, client, screen). The gate-subagent schema accepts only domain|services|persistence|api|tests, so 'services' stands in here. That mismatch between the investigator brief and the hook is a harness gap. Symptom: the FAILs-taken figure that D1 gave to U1 is built from an incomplete verdicts[] on the real trail, and every valid re-review verdict is wrongly listed in problems[]. Cause: src/web/compiler/index.ts:89 reads the round from the file name with /\\/(A\\d+)-([^/]+)\\.json$/. That pattern accepts only A<n>-<agent>.json, but the orchestrator names a same-attempt re-review A<n>.<m>-<agent>.json. So verdictOf returns null at index.ts:91, and index.ts:211 files the verdict as 'the verdict file is not a verdict' instead of pushing it at :212. On docs/trace at HEAD, 22 of the 57 verdict files use the A<n>.<m> form (build/F0b, F2, F3, F4, F5, F6 and ui/U0b). For the build plan the compiler emits 31 of 51 verdicts and 8 of 9 FAILs: it drops docs/trace/build/F5/verdicts/A2.4-reviewer.json (FAIL). That breaks NAV-1 ('attempts and FAILs taken ... from the data') and HONEST-1 (a number that isn't the trail's). U3's LOOP-3 builds on these same records, and its kit already renders 'A3.2' rounds (verdict-card, attempt-ladder), so U3 would inherit the defect. It went undetected because every fixture trail names only A1 and A2 rounds, and nav-1.test.ts:68-79 asserts only those. This is a first diagnosis, not a recurrence of A1's harness cause. It will fire on every future re-review round until the round form is accepted. The rest of the D1 resolution checks clean. data-1.test.ts:84-97 drops only the verdicts assertion, as the steer ruled, and its comment now names U1 as the owner. No test still asserts that verdicts stay empty. docs/ui-requirements.md:418 and ui.dag.yaml:155,178-179 keep U3's LOOP-3 rendering of verdicts, which doesn't conflict with U1 owning the list. Fix direction: treat the round as the whole A<n>[.<m>] token in the file name, and keep it verbatim as the round string (e.g. 'A2.2'), so that a re-review verdict is parsed like any other and no valid verdict reaches problems[]. Then add a fixture case with a re-review round, so the compiler test proves this form.","fingerprint":"NAV-1|src/web/compiler/index.ts|verdict-round-pattern-rejects-rereview-An.m","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a fixture trail whose node has verdicts A1-reviewer.json FAIL, A1-security.json PASS, A1.2-reviewer.json PASS and A1.2-security.json PASS, in the real envelope cut from docs/trace/build/F3/verdicts/A2.2-reviewer.json (a new fixture, or added to the rules fixture with its README figures updated), When the compiler runs, Then verdicts[] holds all four with rounds A1, A1, A1.2, A1.2, their agents, verdicts and files, and problems[] names no verdict file ('NAV-1 · FAILs taken: a re-review round A<n>.<m> is a verdict, not a problem' in tests/web/unit/compiler/nav-1.test.ts)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["10 · A1 · steer(D1,pause1) · David: \"U1 takes verdicts\"; the steer was recorded but no investigator was dispatched (this round is that skipped step)","28 · A1 · gate.coverage FAIL · among its reasons, D1 has no findings","32 · attempt++ → 2; round A1 (findings/A1.md) diagnosed the missing activity record (harness hook outcomes, a different cause from I1 here)"]}
