iler runs Then that commit's rule is [] and #/commits/<short> shows 'no Rule trailer' with no link to #/rules/none (tests/web/unit/compiler/nav-3.test.ts)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["loop.jsonl:10 · A1 · steer(D1,pause1): re-review verdict files A<n>.<m> dropped at index.ts:89; fixed at ffb50b9 (D1/I1)","loop.jsonl:13 · A1 · steer(D2,pause1): compiler fields amended (t6 2160679, t7 640e3e1, t8 709338c); no investigator","loop.jsonl:28,32-33 · A1 · gate.coverage FAIL → attempt 2 (harness-side A1/I1, A1/I2)","loop.jsonl:53,55 · A2 · round D2: six real-data defects (slash ID matrix rows, ui matrix, per-plan figures, merge decisions, 'undefined' cells, template titles) fixed at b70c382 and f64c03f; review A2 PASS both at e8fdf4e","loop.jsonl:58-59 · A2 · t12 QA at 16a258a predicts the D3 failures. None of D3's fingerprints repeats an earlier one, but D1/I1, D2/I1 and D3/I1-I2 share a class: compiler shapes narrower than the real trail, with hand-cut fixtures (JSON-object trailers, no RENEW trait) that cannot express the real shape. The fixture format, not just the parser, has to change."]}
